---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const contactEmail = "me@setkyar.com";
---

<Layout
  title="Waitlist privacy notice — WATeamInbox"
  description="How the WATeamInbox-operated Cloud waitlist collects, uses, retains, and deletes subscriber information."
  imageAlt="WATeamInbox waitlist privacy notice"
>
  <article class="privacy-page">
    <header class="privacy-hero">
      <p class="privacy-kicker"><span aria-hidden="true"></span> WATeamInbox Cloud waitlist</p>
      <h1>Privacy, without the fog.</h1>
      <p class="privacy-lede">
        This notice explains how the operator of <strong>wateaminbox.com</strong>
        handles information submitted to the managed-Cloud waitlist. It does not
        govern independently operated, self-hosted WATeamInbox installations.
      </p>
      <dl class="privacy-facts">
        <div><dt>Last updated</dt><dd>2 August 2026</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Contact</dt><dd><a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Product status</dt><dd>Waitlist only; no Cloud account is created</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </header>

    <div class="privacy-layout">
      <nav aria-label="Privacy notice sections">
        <p>On this page</p>
        <a href="#scope">Scope</a>
        <a href="#data">Information collected</a>
        <a href="#use">How it is used</a>
        <a href="#providers">Service providers</a>
        <a href="#retention">Retention</a>
        <a href="#choices">Your choices</a>
        <a href="#security">Security and changes</a>
      </nav>

      <div class="privacy-content">
        <section id="scope">
          <p class="section-number">01 / scope</p>
          <h2>One small, specific service.</h2>
          <p>
            The WATeamInbox Cloud waitlist records confirmed interest in a
            possible future managed service. Joining does not create a product
            account, start a subscription, or promise a launch date, price,
            feature set, service level, or support entitlement.
          </p>
          <p>
            The operator of <strong>wateaminbox.com</strong> is responsible for
            this waitlist. Questions and privacy requests can be sent to
            <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="data">
          <p class="section-number">02 / information collected</p>
          <h2>What the waitlist stores.</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Email address</strong> submitted through the form.</li>
            <li><strong>Signup and confirmation state</strong>, including relevant timestamps.</li>
            <li><strong>Delivery metadata</strong> needed to send and troubleshoot the confirmation email.</li>
            <li><strong>Pseudonymous security records</strong>, such as keyed hashes used for rate limiting, idempotency, confirmation tokens, and administrator sessions.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Raw confirmation tokens, raw administrator session tokens, and raw
            IP addresses are not stored in the waitlist database. Cloudflare may
            process network, browser, device, and abuse-prevention signals when
            it serves the site, Worker API, email, or Turnstile challenge.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="use">
          <p class="section-number">03 / use</p>
          <h2>Why the information is used.</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Send the double-opt-in confirmation message.</li>
            <li>Record confirmed interest and prevent duplicate or abusive requests.</li>
            <li>Send requested updates about the planned WATeamInbox Cloud service.</li>
            <li>Operate, secure, troubleshoot, and measure the waitlist.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Waitlist information is not sold. It is not used to create a
            WATeamInbox product account. If recurring launch or marketing email
            begins, messages will include an appropriate opt-out mechanism.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="providers">
          <p class="section-number">04 / service providers</p>
          <h2>Where processing happens.</h2>
          <p>
            Cloudflare provides the Pages hosting, Worker runtime, D1 database,
            Turnstile abuse protection, network delivery, and transactional
            Email Service used by this waitlist. Cloudflare processes data under
            its own service terms and privacy documentation and may process it
            in countries where it operates infrastructure.
          </p>
          <p>
            Information may also be disclosed when required by law, to protect
            the service or others, or as part of a legitimate transfer of the
            project where the recipient must continue to respect this notice.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="retention">
          <p class="section-number">05 / retention</p>
          <h2>Kept only for the waitlist purpose.</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Unconfirmed signups</strong> are removed after 30 days of inactivity.</li>
            <li><strong>Confirmed addresses</strong> are retained while the waitlist remains active, unless deletion is requested sooner.</li>
            <li><strong>Rate-limit records</strong> are removed after they become stale; expired confirmation and operational records are cleaned up on a schedule.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            When the waitlist is permanently discontinued and the information
            is no longer needed for its stated purpose or a legal obligation,
            the remaining subscriber records will be deleted.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="choices">
          <p class="section-number">06 / your choices</p>
          <h2>Access, correction, or deletion.</h2>
          <p>
            To ask whether an address is on the waitlist, correct it, withdraw
            from updates, or request deletion, email
            <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}?subject=WATeamInbox%20waitlist%20privacy%20request`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
            Send the request from the subscribed address when possible. The
            operator may ask for reasonable verification before acting so that
            one person cannot access or delete another person's record.
          </p>
          <p>
            Depending on where you live, applicable law may provide additional
            privacy rights or a right to complain to a local regulator. Requests
            may be limited where retention is required by law or needed to
            establish, exercise, or defend legal claims.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="security">
          <p class="section-number">07 / security and changes</p>
          <h2>Practical safeguards, not impossible promises.</h2>
          <p>
            The waitlist uses HTTPS, restricted Cloudflare bindings, double
            opt-in, expiring hashed confirmation tokens, abuse controls, and an
            authenticated administrator view. No system can guarantee absolute
            security. Suspected vulnerabilities should be reported privately to
            <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a> and should not
            include unnecessary personal data.
          </p>
          <p>
            This notice may change when the waitlist, providers, or legal
            obligations change. Material updates will be posted here with a new
            “Last updated” date before they apply to new processing.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy-page {
    --privacy-ink: #15211f;
    --privacy-muted: #586960;
    --privacy-green: #1d633d;
    width: min(100% - 2rem, 74rem);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 7rem) 0 clamp(5rem, 10vw, 8rem);
    color: var(--privacy-ink);
  }
  .privacy-kicker,
  .section-number,
  .privacy-facts dt,
  .privacy-layout nav p,
  .privacy-layout nav a {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .privacy-kicker {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.55rem;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--privacy-green);
  }
  .privacy-kicker span { width: 0.55rem; height: 0.55rem; background: #4d9f62; }
  .privacy-hero { max-width: 58rem; }
  .privacy-hero h1 {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(3.6rem, 8vw, 6.6rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
    line-height: 0.88;
  }
  .privacy-lede {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 1.8rem 0 0;
    color: var(--privacy-muted);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.7vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .privacy-facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
    border: 1px solid #b8c6bc;
    background: #b8c6bc;
  }
  .privacy-facts div { background: #f8f7f1; padding: 1rem; }
  .privacy-facts dt { color: #53715f; }
  .privacy-facts dd { margin: 0.45rem 0 0; color: var(--privacy-ink); font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .privacy-page a { color: var(--privacy-green); }
  .privacy-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 14rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    margin-top: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 7rem);
  }
  .privacy-layout nav { position: sticky; top: 1.5rem; align-self: start; display: grid; gap: 0.75rem; border-top: 1px solid #aebdaf; padding-top: 1rem; }
  .privacy-layout nav p { margin: 0 0 0.35rem; color: #375344; }
  .privacy-layout nav a { color: #63736a; letter-spacing: 0.03em; text-decoration: none; text-transform: none; }
  .privacy-layout nav a:hover { color: var(--privacy-green); }
  .privacy-content { min-width: 0; }
  .privacy-content section { scroll-margin-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid #c8d3c9; padding: 2rem 0 3rem; }
  .section-number { margin: 0; color: #528563; }
  .privacy-content h2 { margin: 0.7rem 0 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 4.5vw, 3.6rem); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.045em; line-height: 0.98; }
  .privacy-content p,
  .privacy-content li { color: var(--privacy-muted); font-size: 0.96rem; line-height: 1.75; }
  .privacy-content p { max-width: 48rem; }
  .privacy-content ul { display: grid; gap: 0.55rem; max-width: 48rem; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .privacy-content strong { color: #294638; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .privacy-facts { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .privacy-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .privacy-layout nav { position: static; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .privacy-layout nav p { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .privacy-page { width: min(100% - 1.5rem, 74rem); }
    .privacy-layout nav { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
